 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c032", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Ultimate net loss\" is defined as the sum \"actually paid or payable\" in settlement or satisfaction, and those two words point in opposite directions on whether the insured must have disbursed money before the company indemnifies. Loss Payable (c054) compounds the question by requiring payment of the underlying limit first.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c033", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Retained Limit\" is the \"greater of\" the total underlying limits or the Item 4 self-insured retention, which leaves it unclear whether the $10,000 retention applies in addition to, or only in the absence of, collectible underlying insurance. The clause's own proviso (\"if the insurance afforded by the underlying insurance is inapplicable\") pulls against the \"greater of\" formula.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c034", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This definition of Personal Injury expressly includes mental anguish, shock, false arrest, libel, slander and invasion of privacy, and (5) racial or religious discrimination, all of which the Personal Injury Endorsement (c064) and the Exclusion of Discrimination (c087) strike out. What \"personal injury\" means in the insuring agreement (c009) cannot be read off this clause alone.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.35}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c035", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Limb (1) requires the physical injury to \"occur during the policy period\" while limb (2) requires only that the loss of use be caused by an occurrence during the period, producing two different triggers within one definition. In a progressive-damage claim the choice of limb decides coverage.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.14}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c036", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c037", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Occurrence\" requires injury \"neither expected nor intended from the standpoint of the insured,\" a subjective-intent standard that is undefined and is applied across multiple insureds under c028-c031. Whether one insured's expectation defeats coverage for others is not addressed.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.25}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c038", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"[A]ll such exposure to substantially the same general conditions existing at or emanating from one location or source shall be deemed one occurrence\" gives no measure for \"substantially the same\" or for what counts as a single \"source.\" The number of occurrences drives the each-occurrence limit in c016.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c039", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c040", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c041", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c042", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The products hazard is stated to include \"personal injury and property damage,\" but the operative proviso then speaks only of \"bodily injury or property damage,\" a term the policy does not define. The mismatch narrows or widens the hazard depending on which phrase is read as controlling.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.14}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c043", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c044", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c045", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c046", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c047", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c048", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c049", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c050", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Notice is due \"as soon as practicable\" once it \"appears that an occurrence is likely to involve indemnity under this policy,\" and neither the trigger nor the deadline has any fixed content. The point at which the insured's duty crystallises on an excess policy is exactly what a late-notice defence would be fought over.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c051", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c052", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c053", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c054", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Liability is said not to attach until the underlying limit \"has been paid by or on behalf of the insured,\" which cannot be squared with Maintenance of Underlying Insurance (c062), under which the policy applies as though unmaintained underlying policies were in force. Whether an unpaid or uncollectible underlying limit blocks attachment is left unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c055", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This Action Against Company condition, including the no-privity sentence, is deleted in its entirety by the Wisconsin Amendatory Endorsement (c074-c076), which substitutes a shorter text permitting \"any person or organization\" to recover. Whether any part of this clause survives is a live question.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c056", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c057", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The assignment sentence is incomplete: it says assignment \"shall not bind\" without stating whom it does not bind or what consent is required, and then runs into an unrelated clause about the unexpired portion of the policy period. As written the restriction has no ascertainable operation.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c058", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This clause makes the policy excess over any other valid and collectible insurance \"whether or not described in the Schedule of Underlying Insurance,\" which pulls against the Retained Limit definition (c033) fixing the attachment point by reference to scheduled limits plus other collectible underlying insurance. Whether unscheduled insurance raises the attachment point or merely shares loss is unclear.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.25}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c059", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The apportionment order set out here reimburses interests that paid in excess of the retained limit first and the company second, but the Wisconsin Subrogation amendment (c077) says the company recovers \"only after the insured has been fully compensated for damages.\" The two orders of priority cannot both be applied.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c060", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This clause says notice to or knowledge of any agent shall not effect a waiver or estop the company, while the Wisconsin Changes endorsement (c078) provides that an agent's knowledge of a fact breaching a condition is the company's knowledge and shall not void the policy. The two provisions are in direct opposition on agent knowledge.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c061", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This condition requires thirty days' written notice of cancellation by the company, while the Cancellation - Wisconsin endorsement (c069-c071) allows ten days and General Amendatory Endorsement No. 3 (c098) requires sixty days. Which notice period governs a cancellation is a direct conflict among three provisions.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.40}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c062", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The warranty to maintain underlying policies, with the saving clause that the policy applies as if they had been maintained, sits against Loss Payable (c054) and the Retained Limit definition (c033), which condition attachment on actual payment of the underlying limit. The consequence of an unmaintained or exhausted underlying policy differs depending on which clause is applied.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c063", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Except insofar as coverage is available to the insured in the underlying insurance listed\" is grammatically incomplete — listed where, and on what date — and it is unclear whether the following-form carve-back tracks the Item 7 schedule or any underlying policy actually in force. The scope of the contractual liability exclusion turns on that missing referent.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c064", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The endorsement preserves coverage \"insofar as coverage is afforded under the underlying insurance or self insured retention listed in Item 7 of the Declarations,\" but Item 7 is the Schedule of Underlying Insurance and the self-insured retention is stated in Item 4. The mis-citation leaves the carve-back's reach uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33}
 ]}
]}

